✅ Advantages

Easy Project Sharing: Share your project with teachers, friends, and developers.

Version Control: Track changes made to your Arduino code.

Backup: Store your project files safely online.

Collaboration: Team members can work together on the project.

Portfolio Building: Showcase your robotics project to potential employers.

Documentation: Add circuit diagrams, code, photos, and project reports.

Open Source Learning: Learn from similar robotics projects.

❌ Disadvantages

Internet Dependency: Internet access is required for convenient online access.

Learning Curve: Beginners may need time to understand Git and GitHub.

Repository Management: Organizing code and documentation requires effort.

Privacy Concerns: Public repositories expose your code to everyone.

Large File Limitations: GitHub has file-size limits for uploads.

Merge Conflicts: Collaboration can sometimes lead to conflicting code changes.
